WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.760
While most spider and scorpion bites cause only mild reactions like some redness and

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:10.960
swelling, certain venomous ones, like the black widow or brown recluse, can make someone

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.520
very ill.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:17.000
Small children and those with existing medical issues are at a higher risk for more severe

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.639
complications, so you'll want to keep a close eye on them.

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:25.520
As you assess the person, watch for signs like muscle cramps, fever, a headache, or

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:29.120
more serious issues like difficulty breathing or fainting.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.919
If you notice severe symptoms like trouble breathing, intense pain, or an altered mental

00:00:33.919 --> 00:00:36.880
status, call 911 immediately.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.720
For most situations, your immediate care is to wash the wound with soap and water and

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:44.320
apply an ice pack to manage the discomfort.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:48.400
For children, it is always a good idea to follow up by calling poison control or their

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.840
health care provider for further guidance.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:56.040
Finally, if you can do so safely and without touching the insect, try to take a photo of

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.040
it.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:01.360
It can be incredibly helpful for medical professionals to identify exactly what caused

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.720
the bite and determine the best treatment.

